# Platform constraints

Recorded because each cost time and none are documented where you would look.
Multi-Framework reached GA in 2026; the tooling is young.

## Apex REST requires a CSRF token

Salesforce's documentation says to call Apex REST "with fetch". Their SDK's
`csrf/header.interceptor` states Apex REST endpoints are protected on **all**
methods. A bare `fetch()` returns **403**.

**Use the SDK's `fetch` via `createDataSDK()`.** The interceptor supplies the
token. The documentation is wrong.

## `@AuraEnabled` is unreachable from React

Only Apex REST endpoints are callable from a UI Bundle. Hence
`AOS_RestBridge` — structural, not a workaround. See `03-aos-rest-bridge`.

## The local dev proxy cannot forward POSTs

`@salesforce/ui-bundle`'s proxy fails with
`InvalidArgumentError: invalid content-length header` (undici,
`UND_ERR_INVALID_ARG`) in `UIBundleProxyHandler.handleSalesforceApi`.

Reproduced from a clean scaffold on Node 22 and 24, with and without our
`.npmrc`, in two separate repos. **Consequence: no local development against
the org.** Work on build-and-deploy cycles.

Unreported to Salesforce at time of writing.

## Two project roots

- **`npm` commands** run in `force-app/main/default/uiBundles/<name>/`
- **`sf` commands** run at the project root

The root `package.json` is the base SFDX template and its `build` script does
nothing. Keep two terminal tabs.

## UIBundle and CustomApplication are mutually dependent

The bundle targets the app; the app names the bundle. **Deploy both in one
command** or neither resolves. Separate deploys fail with an unhelpful error.

## StrictMode runs effects twice in development

Two identical requests in the Network tab is expected, not a bug.

## GraphQL has no aggregation

No `COUNT`, `SUM` or `GROUP BY`. Anything aggregate goes through a processor.

## UI API mutations are single-record

No transaction across two mutations. Multi-object writes go through a processor.

## Screen flows are not callable from Apex

Only autolaunched flows. Reusing screen-flow logic means extracting it into an
autolaunched flow first.
